XX
Names: Bms1-type guanine nucleotide-binding (G) domain
Function: Bms1p and Tsr1p represent a new family of factors required for
 ribosome biogenesis. They are each independently required for 40S ribosomal
 subunit biogenesis. Bms1p, a protein required for pre-rRNA processing,
 contains an evolutionarily conserved G domain with five conserved polypeptide
 loops designated G1 through G5, which form contact sites with the guanine
 nucleotide or coordinate the Mg(2+) ion. Tsr1p lacks a P-loop and is not
 predicted to bind GTP.
XX
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the TRAFAC class translation factor GTPase
CC       superfamily. Bms1-like GTPase family.
