Names: GB1/RHD3-type guanine nucleotide-binding (G) domain
Function: The GB1/RHD3 GTPase family contains a large G domain (~230 amino
 acids). The GB1/RHD3-type G domain has a low intrinsic affinity for
 nucleotide and often depends on nucleotide-dependent homodimerization to
 facilitate GTP hydrolysis.
