XX
Names: LCN-type cysteine-stabilized alpha/beta (CS-alpha/beta) domain
Function: Most long-chain neurotoxins (LCNs) are composed of 60-70 residues
 and are cross-linked by four disulphide bridges. The long chain or voltage-
 gated sodium channels scorpion neurotoxins (NaScTxs) can be classified either
 as alpha-toxins, which slow down Na(+) channel inactivation, or beta-toxins,
 which affect the channel activation process.
