Function: The degenerated Gid-type RING finger is characterized by an
 incomplete series of Zn(2+) ion-ccordinating residues compared with the
 canonical RING finger, which encompasses eight Cys/His residues coordinating
 two Zn cations. A complete cysteine and histidine pattern is not necessarily
 critical for the E3 function.
