XX
Names: CENP-V/GFA domain
Function: At the C-terminal end, CENP-V possesses an evolutionally conserved
 domain that comprises an array of seven cysteines and shows high structural
 similarity to glutathione-dependent formaldehyde-activating enzyme (Gfa), an
 enzyme responsible for formaldehyde detoxification in prokaryotes. CENP-V
 could be an enzyme that scavenges the formaldehyde produced in histone
 demethylation reactions.
