Function: Subtilases are an extensive family of serine proteases which occur
 in Archaea, Bacteria, fungi, yeasts, and higher eukaryotes. Their catalytic
 activity is provided by a charge relay system similar to that of the trypsin
 family of serine proteases but which evolved by independent convergent
 evolution.
