XX
Names: Alt a 1 (AA1)-like domain
Function: AA1-like proteins are fungal toxins that can induce plant defense
 responses and cell death. They may contribute to virulence by protecting the
 cell wall, thus allowing fungal growth to be maintained and preventing the
 recognition of degraded beta-1,3-glucan by the plant. AA1 proteins comprise
 ~150 amino acids and contain two pairs of highly conserved disulfide bonds.
XX
