AC   PRU01245;
DC   Domain;
TR   PROSITE; PS51897; ANNEXIN_2; 1; level=0
XX
Names: Annexin repeat
Function: Annexins are a group of calcium-binding proteins that associate
 reversibly with membranes. Each of these proteins consist of a unique N-
 terminal domain followed by four or eight copies (in annexin A6) of a
 conserved segment of approximately 70 residues. Each of the repeats has the
 potential to have a type II Ca(2+)-binding bipartite motif, located on two
 different alpha-helices (GxGT-(38-40 residues)-D/E), but typically some of
 them are non-functional.
XX
