XX
Names: Invertebrate (I)-type lysozyme domain
Function: I-type lysozymes have been identified in phylogenetically diverse
 organisms, including mollusca, nematoda, annelida, arthropoda and
 echinodermata. I-type lysozymes play an important role in immunity and
 digestion in invertebrates and are usually regarded as the first barrier
 against pathogens. I-type lysozymes exert multiple activities, such as
 muramidase, isopeptidase, chitinase, and non-enzymatic antibacterial
 activities.
XX
