AC   PRU01282;
DC   Domain;
TR   PROSITE; PS51353; ARSC; 1; level=0
XX
Names: ArsC family
Function: ArsC is an ~150-residue arsenate reductase that uses reduced
 glutathione (GSH) to convert arsenate to arsenite with a redox active
 cysteine residue in the active site. The arsC family also comprises the Spx
 proteins which are GRAM-positive bacterial transcription factors that
 regulate the transcription of multiple genes in response to disulfide stress.
XX
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the ArsC family.
XX
