AC   PRU01285;
DC   Domain;
TR   PROSITE; PS51936; POU_4; 1; level=0
XX
Names: POU-specific (POUs) atypical domain
Function: HNF1alpha (MODY3 gene product, the most commonly mutated MODY
 protein) and HNF1beta (hepatocyte nuclear factor 1beta; also known as vHNF1
 or TCF2) (MODY5 gene product) are atypical members of the POU transcription
 factors. Their atypical POUs domains have at least one additional alpha-helix
 at the N-terminus, and the second helix and adjacent loop of their POUh
 domains are much longer, creating a more extensive interface between the POUs
 and POUh domains.
XX
