XX
Names: Grh/CP2 DNA-binding (DB) domain
Function: Grh/CP2 transcription factors (TFs) are highly conserved in
 multicellular organisms as key regulators of epithelial differentiation,
 organ development and skin barrier formation. Members of this TF family are
 widely found in diverse taxa, ranging from fungi to animals. All Grh/CP2
 family members share a common domain architecture characterized by an
 intrinsically unstructured N-terminal transactivation domain (TAD), a
 conserved DNA-binding domain (DBD), also termed CP2 binding domain, and a C-
 terminal dimerization domain (DD).
XX
