XX
Names: PBC domain
Function: The PBC class of TALE homeodomain proteins includes the products of
 the vertebrate Pbx1, Pbx2, Pbx3 and Pbx4, Caenorhabditis elegans ceh-20,
 ceh-40 and ceh-60 and the Drosophila extradenticle (exd) genes. The sequence
 similarity between the PBC proteins extends downstream of the homeodomain for
 about 15 amino acids, and upstream of the homeodomain is a 180-amino acid
 dimerization domain termed PBC. The PBC domain can be further subdivided into
 an A and B region.
