AC   PRU01364;
DC   Domain;
TR   PROSITE; PS52020; CRESS_DNA_REP; 1; level=0
XX
Names: CRESS-DNA virus replication initiator protein (Rep) endonuclease domain
Function: The Rep endonuclease domain is characterized by rolling circle
 replication (RCR) motifs I through III, which are important for RCR
 initiation and termination. Motif I, UUTU (U denotes hydrophobic residues),
 is thought to be involved in the recognition of the origin of replication.
 Motif II, HU(H/Q), is involved in the coordination of divalent metal ions,
 Mg(2+) or Mn(2+), which are essential for endonuclease activity at the origin
 of replication. Motif III (YxxK, where x is any amino acid) is involved in
 dsDNA cleavage and subsequent covalent attachment of the Rep through the
 catalytic tyrosine residue to the 5' end of the cleaved product.
XX
