AC   PRU01369;
DC   Domain;
TR   PROSITE; PS52025; GL_BHV; 1; level=0
XX
Names: Betaherpesvirus glycoprotein L (gL) domain
Function: Two glycoprotein complexes are conserved throughout the three
 herpesvirus subfamilies: the trimeric glycoprotein B (gB) that functions as a
 membrane fusogen and the heterodimeric glycoprotein H/glycoprotein L (gH/gL),
 the role of which is less clearly defined. The intrinsic structural
 plasticity of gH/gL enables it to function as a signal integration machine
 that can accept diverse regulatory inputs and convert them into a "trigger"
 signal that activates the fusogenic ability of gB.
XX
DE   + AltName: Full=Envelope glycoprotein L;
DE            Short=gL;
XX
