XX
Names: Streptococcal M proteins C repeat
Function: M proteins belong to a family of fibrous streptococcal surface
 proteins which represent major virulence factors due to their antiphagocytic
 activities. The C repeats are present in all M proteins, although the number
 of repeat sequences varies from two (M6) to four (M12). The conserved
 repetitive C units are responsible for several biological activities of M and
 M-like proteins.
