AC   PRU01374;
DC   Domain;
TR   PROSITE; PS52030; SMDRR; 1; level=0
XX
Names: Streptococcal M proteins D repeat
Function: M proteins belong to a family of fibrous streptococcal surface
 proteins which represent major virulence factors due to their antiphagocytic
 activities. All M proteins share a common framework that includes a conserved
 signal peptide, a hypervariable amino terminus, a less variable central
 domain, and a highly conserved C-terminus. A number of repeat sequences (A,
 B, C and D repeats) follow the hypervariable region. Sequence conservation
 increases from the A repeats to D repeats.
XX
CC   -!- SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Secreted, cell wall; Peptidoglycan-anchor.
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the M protein family.
