XX
Names: Vms1-like release factor 1 (VLRF1) domain
Function: The ANKZF1/Vms1 Vms1-like release factor 1 (VLRF1) domain, which
 acts as a peptidyl-tRNA hydrolase, has a catalytic loop bearing a conserved
 glutamine. In addition to the glutamine in the active site, the VLRF1 domain
 also contains conserved vicinal arginines in the alpha-helix immediately
 following the active-site loop. The cleavage mechanism involves remodelling
 and cleavage of the ribose-phosphate backbone of the tRNA by a tyrosine and
 the GSQ motif.
XX
