Names: Bacterial ISG15-like (Bil) ubiquitin-like domain
Function: One antiphage defense system in bacteria, comprises a ubiquitin-like
 protein, ubiquitin-conjugating enzymes E1 and E2, and a deubiquitinase. Owing
 to its double-UBL domain and role in antiviral defense, the system was coined
 "Bil" (bacterial ISG15-like), and is composed of BilA/B/C/D encoding UBL, E2,
 DUB, and E1 modules, respectively.
