AC   PRU01412;
DC   Domain;
TR   PROSITE; PS52066; MCM10_CTD; 1; level=0
XX
Names: MCM10 C-terminal domain (MCM10-CTD)
Function: The MCM10 CTD, although not present in unicellular eukaryotes, is
 conserved among metazoan species from nematodes to humans. The CTD contains a
 winged helix domain (WH) and two zinc chelating motifs, a CCCH zinc-finger
 (ZnF2) and a CCCC zinc-ribbon (ZnR). ssDNA binds only to ZnF2, whose
 structure is unique to MCM10. The ZnR is not involved in DNA binding.
XX
CC   -!- SIMILARITY: Belongs to the MCM10 family.
