Names: GPN-loop GTPase domain
Function: GPN-loop GTPases are assembly chaperones for RNA polymerase II (Pol
 II) and other protein complexes. This family of conserved GTPases has been
 named GPN-loop GTPases due to the presence of a conserved Gly-Pro-Asn motif
 inserted into the GTPase core-fold. GPN-loop GTPases form homo- and
 heterodimers.
