AC   PRU01417;
DC   Domain;
TR   PROSITE; PS52072; VPS10P; 1; level=0
XX
Names: Vacuolar protein sorting 10 protein (Vps10p) domain
Function: The Vps10p domain is formed by three structural units: a large N-
 terminal beta-propeller and two cysteine-knots called 10CCa and 10CCb, which
 constitute the so-called 10CC (ten conserved cysteines) module. The Vps10p
 propeller has a wide, open tunnel lined by ten edge strands running parallel
 to the propeller axis, thus providing ample opportunity for beta-sheet
 extension to capture extended peptides threaded into the tunnel. The C-
 terminal elongated 10CC module that partly wraps around the 'bottom' face of
 the propeller contains five conserved disulfide bridges and is a major
 ligand-binding region.
XX
KW   Receptor
KW   Transport
KW   Protein transport
case <FTTag:disulf>
KW   Disulfide bond
end case
XX
